{
  "_ulid": "01KJZQRKK3DJQ0KSDT7EZ2V892",
  "slugs": [
    "task-dispatch-daemon-guard"
  ],
  "title": "Prevent dispatch agents from killing host daemon",
  "type": "task",
  "description": "Dispatch worker agents can accidentally kill the daemon hosting the dispatch engine by running kspec serve stop/restart. This happened in practice during fix cycle 4 of @implement-task-board-kanban — the agent tried to debug E2E failures by manually starting a daemon, which killed the dispatch daemon and severed the WebSocket connection.\n\nFix requires two changes:\n1. Inject KSPEC_DAEMON_PID into spawned agent environment (in invocation.ts alongside KSPEC_SESSION_ID)\n2. Guard kspec serve stop/restart/start to refuse when KSPEC_DAEMON_PID is set, with clear error message\n\nAlso update agent instructions to add convention: never run kspec serve stop/restart/start when running under dispatch.",
  "spec_ref": "@cli-serve-commands",
  "meta_ref": null,
  "plan_ref": null,
  "status": "pending_review",
  "blocked_by": [],
  "depends_on": [],
  "context": [],
  "priority": 2,
  "tags": [
    "cli",
    "dispatch",
    "bug"
  ],
  "vcs_refs": [],
  "created_at": "2026-03-05T19:32:00.739Z",
  "started_at": "2026-03-05T19:32:39.048Z",
  "submitted_at": "2026-03-05T19:51:24.385Z",
  "notes": [
    {
      "_ulid": "01KJZQS871W22QPR27A6TZDXTA",
      "created_at": "2026-03-05T19:32:21.857Z",
      "author": "@claude",
      "content": "Spec coverage: spans two specs:\n- @cli-serve-commands ac-11 (new): guard serve stop/restart/start when KSPEC_DAEMON_PID is set\n- @agent-invocation-lifecycle ac-12 (new): inject KSPEC_DAEMON_PID into agent env\n\nImplementation approach:\n1. In src/agent-runtime/invocation.ts: add KSPEC_DAEMON_PID to the env object alongside KSPEC_SESSION_ID (get daemon PID from PidFileManager or process.ppid)\n2. In src/cli/commands/serve.ts: add guard at top of stopServer() and restartServer() checking process.env.KSPEC_DAEMON_PID, refuse with error message\n3. In startServer(): also guard — if KSPEC_DAEMON_PID is set, the agent shouldn't be trying to start daemons either\n4. Update kspec-agents.md development convention to warn about this\n\nFiles to modify:\n- src/agent-runtime/invocation.ts (env injection)\n- src/cli/commands/serve.ts (guard in stop/restart/start)\n- templates/agents-sections/ or kspec meta (add convention rule)",
      "supersedes": null,
      "superseded": false
    },
    {
      "_ulid": "01KJZRVWQ54NMW6KDXPD55QWNQ",
      "created_at": "2026-03-05T19:51:16.965Z",
      "author": "@claude",
      "content": "Implementation complete (500377d60):\n- Added guardAgentContext() to src/cli/commands/serve.ts — checks KSPEC_SESSION_ID at top of startServer, stopServer, restartServer\n- 4 tests in tests/cli-serve.test.ts covering start/stop/restart refusal + JSON error output\n- Convention rule added to kspec-agents.md via kspec meta\n- All 26 serve tests pass (0 regressions)\n- No changes needed to invocation.ts — KSPEC_SESSION_ID already injected for all agent spawns\n- Removed unnecessary ac-12 from @agent-invocation-lifecycle (KSPEC_DAEMON_PID not needed)",
      "supersedes": null,
      "superseded": false
    }
  ],
  "todos": [],
  "automation": "eligible",
  "_sourceFile": "/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml",
  "inherited_traits": [
    {
      "ref": "@trait-json-output",
      "title": "JSON Output Mode",
      "acceptance_criteria": [
        {
          "id": "ac-1",
          "given": "command supports JSON mode",
          "when": "--json flag is provided",
          "then": "output is valid JSON with no ANSI color codes"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-2",
          "given": "JSON mode is active",
          "when": "command completes successfully",
          "then": "output includes all data available in human-readable mode"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-3",
          "given": "JSON mode is active",
          "when": "command encounters an error",
          "then": "error is returned as JSON object with error field"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-4",
          "given": "JSON output contains references",
          "when": "output is generated",
          "then": "references use @ prefix consistently"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-5",
          "given": "JSON output contains timestamps",
          "when": "output is generated",
          "then": "timestamps use ISO 8601 format"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-6",
          "given": "command supports --json",
          "when": "used with other formatting flags",
          "then": "--json takes precedence over other format options"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "@trait-semantic-exit-codes",
      "title": "Semantic Exit Codes",
      "acceptance_criteria": [
        {
          "id": "ac-1",
          "given": "command completes successfully",
          "when": "operation succeeds",
          "then": "exit code 0"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-2",
          "given": "command encounters validation error",
          "when": "user input is invalid",
          "then": "exit code 1"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-3",
          "given": "command is cancelled by user",
          "when": "confirmation prompt declined",
          "then": "exit code 2"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-4",
          "given": "command encounters runtime error",
          "when": "operation fails during execution",
          "then": "exit code 3"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-5",
          "given": "command finds nothing",
          "when": "query returns no results",
          "then": "exit code 0 with empty result set"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-6",
          "given": "command used incorrectly",
          "when": "invalid flags or arguments provided",
          "then": "exit code 1 with usage information"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-7",
          "given": "batch operation completes",
          "when": "partial failures occur",
          "then": "exit code 1"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-8",
          "given": "command documentation",
          "when": "developers implement commands",
          "then": "exit code meanings documented in code"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "@trait-error-guidance",
      "title": "Error Messages with Recovery Guidance",
      "acceptance_criteria": [
        {
          "id": "ac-1",
          "given": "command encounters error",
          "when": "error message is shown",
          "then": "includes description of what went wrong"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-2",
          "given": "command encounters error",
          "when": "error message is shown",
          "then": "includes suggested action to resolve"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-3",
          "given": "reference not found",
          "when": "error is shown",
          "then": "suggests checking ref with kspec search or kspec <type> list"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-4",
          "given": "invalid state transition",
          "when": "error is shown",
          "then": "indicates current state and valid next states"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-5",
          "given": "validation error",
          "when": "error is shown",
          "then": "indicates which field/value failed validation"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-6",
          "given": "error in JSON mode",
          "when": "--json is active",
          "then": "guidance included in structured error object"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

